38:Tcf1,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a split train journey?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A split journey divides a longer train trip into two or more distinct segments connected via an intermediate railway junction. Instead of travelling end-to-end on a single direct train, you travel on one train to a transfer station and switch to a connecting train to reach your final destination."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why do split journeys have seat availability when direct trains are waitlisted?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Direct long-distance trains usually exhaust their end-to-end quota quickly because travellers book the full corridor. However, intermediate segments and regional trains often have unallocated seats or separate booking quotas. By splitting the journey at a major junction, travellers can tap into available inventory on individual legs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a split journey guarantee a confirmed seat?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Trayago surfaces feasible connecting combinations and the seat availability reported by reservation systems at the time of your search. Railway quotas and booking status fluctuate in real time, and ticket confirmation is determined solely by Indian Railways at the time of purchase."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the primary risks of booking a split journey?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The primary operational risk is a missed connection. If your first train suffers an unexpected delay and arrives after your second train departs, the second train will not wait. To minimize this risk, Trayago encourages selecting generous layover buffer times (at least 1.5 to 3 hours) and checking live running status before travelling."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need separate tickets for each leg of a split journey?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Each leg is operated as an independent train service with its own PNR, coach allocation, quota, and fare. You must purchase a separate ticket for each train leg on official booking channels like IRCTC."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a split journey cheaper than a direct train ticket?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not necessarily. In many cases, booking two separate tickets incurs two base fare calculations and reservation fees, which can make the total cost slightly higher than a single direct ticket. The main benefit of a split journey is route availability when through trains are sold out, not price savings."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I book railway tickets directly on Trayago?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Trayago is an independent journey intelligence and route planning platform. We do not issue railway tickets, process ticket booking payments, or act as an IRCTC booking agent. Once you find a suitable route, tickets must be booked through official portals such as IRCTC."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Trayago affiliated with IRCTC or Indian Railways?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Trayago is an independent platform and has no affiliation with, endorsement from, or official relationship with IRCTC or the Ministry of Railways, Government of India."}}]}15:["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://www.trayago.in\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"AI Split Journey\",\"item\":\"https://www.trayago.in/split-journey\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"name\":\"AI Split Train Journey Planner — Alternative Route Discovery\",\"url\":\"https://www.trayago.in/split-journey\",\"description\":\"Learn how split train ticketing works on Indian Railways. Trayago's AI Split Journey engine evaluates intermediate railway junction combinations when direct trains are waitlisted.\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"name\":\"Trayago\",\"url\":\"https://www.trayago.in\"}}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$38"}}],"$L39"],null,"$L3a"]}]
